  <h3>Skills and Competencies Developed</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Software Design and Engineering:</strong> By improving the Contact Service Appointment Project, I refined validation logic, exception handling, and unit tests, producing more maintainable, professional-quality code. 
        For example, I implemented stricter input validation rules to ensure names were between 1–10 characters and phone numbers exactly 10 digits, reducing potential errors and ensuring data integrity. 
        I also refactored error handling to provide meaningful messages while keeping internal system details secure.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Algorithms and Data Structures:</strong> Enhancements to data storage using <code>HashMap</code> and regex validation demonstrated algorithmic thinking and efficient use of data structures for performance and reliability. 
        Using a <code>HashMap</code> allowed O(1) access, insert, and deletion operations, significantly improving the efficiency of contact management compared to previous linear search approaches. 
        Regex validation for phone numbers and address formatting strengthened data sanitization practices.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Database Development:</strong> Enhancing the <code>AnimalShelterCRUD</code> class improved CRUD operations, introduced input validation, flexible connection handling, and batch operations, reflecting secure, scalable, and maintainable database design. 
        These improvements make the database layer robust and ready for real-world applications.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Professional Communication:</strong> Improved documentation, comments, and structured narratives ensured that both code and explanations are clear, thorough, and understandable to other developers and stakeholders. 
        Inline comments in Java and docstrings in Python provide context for future collaborators, demonstrating professional coding practices.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Problem Solving and Critical Thinking:</strong> Challenges such as managing boundary cases, balancing validation with usability, and ensuring secure coding practices strengthened my analytical and problem-solving skills. 
        One example involved ensuring batch updates in the database did not unintentionally affect other records, which required careful testing and iterative debugging. 
        Another involved balancing strict validation with user flexibility, which taught me to make thoughtful design trade-offs.
    </li>
  </ul>

